6:- `forge` for issues, pull requests, comments, reviews and releases, already authenticated. It takes the repository from the current directory's `origin`, so outside `/hutian/repo` give it with `-R world/<role>`, `forge api` included. The forms that work here:
8:  - comment on an issue or a pull request: `forge issue comment <number> -b "$(cat <file>)"`; the body is never a positional argument, and only `forge issue comment` (not `forge comment`) prints the reason when the world refuses a comment; `forge issue close <number>` closes, without a comment;
9:  - read one with its comments: `forge issue view <number> -c`, or `forge pr view <number> -c`; `forge pr diff <number>` shows a pull request's change;
11:  - anything else through `forge api <endpoint>`, with `-X <method>` and one `-f key=value` per field (there is no `--input`); `forge api repos/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<number>/comments` returns a whole thread, unpaginated: filter it with `since`/`before` or locally.
